---
description: React application, API-consumer, localization, and frontend validation rules
globs:
  - "src/**/*.js"
  - "src/**/*.jsx"
  - "src/**/*.ts"
  - "src/**/*.tsx"
  - "scripts/**/*.js"
  - "package.json"
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use npm and keep `package-lock.json`; do not generate pnpm/yarn lockfiles.
- Keep API changes backward-compatible during staggered releases and update all affected consumers/tests.
- Client-side route or component gating improves UX but never replaces backend permission checks.
- Preserve URL attribution, accessibility, responsive behavior, explicit website publication, and localization dictionary parity.
- Never expose draft website data publicly or claim Google/provider state based only on local React state.
- Run focused tests with `CI=true npm test -- --runInBand --watch=false <paths>`, lint changed files, and run `npm run build` for routing/configuration/cross-cutting UI changes.
